{
  "laswell_spec_version": 1,
  "id": "0070-seed-room",
  "description": "Seed the eleven rooms of the house.",
  "rationale": "Written as literal values rather than a select, so the rows themselves are inside the signature and readable in the ledger afterwards. Ids are explicit because every item seed refers to them by number; overriding system is what PostgreSQL requires to write a GENERATED ALWAYS identity, and pg_laswell follows the insert with the setval that stops the next application insert colliding. area_m2 is written as a string: floating-point values are refused anywhere in a specification, and numeric(6,2) is not a float -- sending it as one would round-trip through a double on the way to the signature.",
